# Rule 1: Backend and console boundaries

The user works on the backend (`apps/worker`, `packages/**`) and the console (`apps/console`).

## Backend
- `apps/worker/**`
- `packages/**` (`db`, `domain`, `contracts`, `integrations`, `crawling`, `config`)
- Prisma schema/migrations (Neon **dev** branch only; never prod)
- Keep shared contracts backward compatible.

## Console (`apps/console`)
- Next.js App Router + Tailwind + shadcn-style UI kit + TanStack Query.
- Talks to the backend only through its server-side proxy (`app/api/proxy/[...path]`), never directly from the browser.
- May import `@moncha/contracts` (zod schemas and types). Never import `@moncha/db`, `@moncha/domain`, `@moncha/crawling` or `@moncha/integrations`, and never connect to the database.
- If a screen needs data the API does not return, add the endpoint to the backend first.

## Environment
- Backend env lives in `apps/worker/.env` (template: `apps/worker/.env.example`). It is the only env file the backend reads: the worker (`apps/worker/src/env.ts`), the Prisma CLI (`packages/db/prisma.config.ts`) and the guarded db scripts (`packages/db/scripts/guarded.cjs`).
- Console env lives in `apps/console/.env.local` (template: `apps/console/.env.example`).
- Never print secret values; show keys only.
